<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Llucmajor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">25 October 1349</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Llucmajor was fought on 25 October 1349 near Llucmajor in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a>. James III, the deposed king of Majorca, landed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> to retake his kingdom from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iv-of-aragon">Peter IV of Aragon</a>, but was defeated and killed by the Aragonese army. His death ended all hope of restoring the independent Kingdom of Majorca.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-llucmajor.jpg" alt="Battle of Llucmajor" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antoni Salvà · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rei_Jaume_III_Llucmajor_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
